{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00343",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.18,
      "end_seconds": 3.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Excuse me, doctor, should I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.33,
      "end_seconds": 7.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Yes, do sit. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 8.44,
      "end_seconds": 11.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.66,
      "end_seconds": 14.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.56,
      "end_seconds": 24.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.67,
      "text": "Um, so... a tight band-like headache. That's why I came. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.38,
      "end_seconds": 29.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "And when did that start? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.37,
      "end_seconds": 37.95,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "About... well, about a year. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.29,
      "end_seconds": 42.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Right, how would you describe it, mild, moderate, severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.37,
      "end_seconds": 48.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.92,
      "end_seconds": 54.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.04,
      "end_seconds": 57.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "It's mild, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.67,
      "end_seconds": 59.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Alright. Anything that helps?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.51,
      "end_seconds": 63.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "It settles a little with rest and a head massage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.68,
      "end_seconds": 69.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 69.2,
      "end_seconds": 74.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, uh, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.24,
      "end_seconds": 78.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "So, I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.81,
      "end_seconds": 84.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything. Has there been tired eyes too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.08,
      "end_seconds": 89.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Right, you know, yes, about the same, four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.16,
      "end_seconds": 94.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "So, have you had pain in the neck and shoulders?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.84,
      "end_seconds": 96.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Yeah, that too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.67,
      "end_seconds": 100.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.33,
      "end_seconds": 107.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.0,
      "end_seconds": 113.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.53,
      "end_seconds": 115.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "It's severe, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.72,
      "end_seconds": 121.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Alright, have you had a tight band-like headache before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.65,
      "end_seconds": 127.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "A bit, about six months ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 127.81,
      "end_seconds": 131.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Yes, that's right, that's how it was."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.37,
      "end_seconds": 134.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Any jaw pain when chewing, numbness or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.83,
      "end_seconds": 147.44,
      "duration_seconds": 11.61,
      "text": "So, no, no jaw pain when chewing, no numbness, no vomiting. I did have irritability at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.95,
      "end_seconds": 150.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Any blurred vision, fever or weakness at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.99,
      "end_seconds": 153.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "No. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.3,
      "end_seconds": 157.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "So, anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.05,
      "end_seconds": 160.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.97,
      "end_seconds": 163.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.99,
      "end_seconds": 169.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.6,
      "end_seconds": 173.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.55,
      "end_seconds": 179.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "Escitalopram. I take it 10 milligrams, once a day for the anxiety."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 181.03,
      "end_seconds": 188.05,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the escitalopram was 20 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.41,
      "end_seconds": 191.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "I see. Is the most recent prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.47,
      "end_seconds": 202.04,
      "duration_seconds": 9.57,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Paracetamol. I take it 500 milligrams, when needed. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.54,
      "end_seconds": 205.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "So, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.57,
      "end_seconds": 209.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "I mean, just a hernia repair, about five years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.6,
      "end_seconds": 216.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.88,
      "end_seconds": 225.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.9,
      "text": "Okay, so I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.75,
      "end_seconds": 229.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.37,
      "end_seconds": 244.55,
      "duration_seconds": 13.18,
      "text": "I've had anxiety, yes. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. I've had high blood pressure, yes. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.91,
      "end_seconds": 246.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.53,
      "end_seconds": 251.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Okay, anxiety, that's already on your record. Good to know. Right, do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.93,
      "end_seconds": 255.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "I stopped smoking about two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.96,
      "end_seconds": 258.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.42,
      "end_seconds": 262.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.15,
      "end_seconds": 266.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.02,
      "end_seconds": 269.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "So, my father was diabetic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.49,
      "end_seconds": 274.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.51,
      "end_seconds": 276.34,
      "duration_seconds": 0.83,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.43,
      "end_seconds": 290.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.73,
      "end_seconds": 294.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.2,
      "end_seconds": 295.9,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.79,
      "end_seconds": 298.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Open wide for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.24,
      "end_seconds": 318.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Your eye movements and reflexes are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.86,
      "end_seconds": 321.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.37,
      "end_seconds": 325.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Now I'm going to check this part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.52,
      "end_seconds": 340.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "The muscles at the back of your neck are tight and tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.06,
      "end_seconds": 362.09,
      "duration_seconds": 17.03,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. So, based on the history and the examination, this looks most like a tension-type headache. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I can't rule out migraine yet. I can't rule out a medication-overuse headache yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.25,
      "end_seconds": 366.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Uh, is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.6,
      "end_seconds": 381.74,
      "duration_seconds": 14.14,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a tension-type headache do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a tight band-like headache for about a year, mild, and no weakness or vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.56,
      "end_seconds": 387.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.32,
      "end_seconds": 395.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an eye check for headache and eye strain. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.57,
      "end_seconds": 397.53,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.11,
      "end_seconds": 422.72,
      "duration_seconds": 23.61,
      "text": "Let's use amitriptyline, 10 milligrams, at night, for six weeks. That should help with headache prevention. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Painkillers on most days can actually make the headaches stick around. Take a break from the screen every hour and do a few neck stretches. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 423.77,
      "end_seconds": 439.39,
      "duration_seconds": 15.62,
      "text": "Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. We'll refer you to physiotherapy. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0072",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 440.76,
      "end_seconds": 442.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0073",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 442.64,
      "end_seconds": 449.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0074",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 451.79,
      "end_seconds": 453.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0075",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 454.19,
      "end_seconds": 456.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Let's review you in a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0076",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 456.85,
      "end_seconds": 461.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0077",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 461.74,
      "end_seconds": 464.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0078",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 465.66,
      "end_seconds": 467.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Thanks so much, doctor."
    }
  ]
}